        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"stael-corinne-e62ac46f822afd63\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.96,\"analysis\":\"Corinne’s embedded clause “puisque je vous aime” straightforwardly presents her love for Oswald as a true emotional state and as the reason she believes she could follow him and become his companion. The surrounding emotion does not independently make the clause an expressive/reflexive discharge. Nor does this clause itself undertake a commitment: Corinne gives an explicit promise only in her subsequent speech.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The clause helps answer a question about becoming Oswald’s life companion, but its grammatical and pragmatic role is evidential—giving love as her reason—rather than independently promissory.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Corinne directly addresses Oswald in dialogue; “je vous aime” is embedded as the causal ground in her reply, “Je le crois, puisque je vous aime.”\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Oswald asks whether Corinne would follow him to Scotland and be his life companion. She answers that she believes she would because she loves him. Their tears, music, and heightened emotion intensify the scene but do not show that the love clause is reflexively blurted or discharged. The text distinguishes this avowal from the ensuing undertaking: after Oswald asks her to conceal nothing, Corinne separately consents and says that her promise is given, subject to a delay.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Je le crois, répondit Corinne, je le crois, puisque je vous aime.”\",\"supports\":\"The love clause is an affirmative avowal presented as the reason for Corinne’s belief that she could follow Oswald and be his companion, strongly supporting T.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Oswald asks: “Me suivrais-tu…? Serais-tu la digne compagne de ma vie…?”\",\"supports\":\"Establishes that Corinne’s reply concerns a possible shared life, while the causal form of the love clause supplies a reason rather than itself explicitly undertaking that future.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Immediately afterward Corinne says, “j’y souscris. Ma promesse est donnée; je n’y mets qu’une condition…”\",\"supports\":\"The separate, explicit promise indicates that commitment force belongs primarily to the subsequent utterance, not to “je vous aime” itself.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Before the exchange, both characters yield to tears under the influence of the Scottish painting, songs, and memories.\",\"supports\":\"Shows intense emotional framing, but supplies no positive evidence that Corinne’s particular words function as an involuntary or reflex-like expressive discharge.\",\"confidence\":0.95},{\"evidence_id\":\"e5\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The occurrence is marked as affirmative present-tense “je vous aime” in Chapter IV of Madame de Staël’s Corinne; ou, l’Italie.\",\"supports\":\"Confirms the identified affirmative present love construction and its bibliographic location.\",\"confidence\":0.99}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the clause as an avowal of loving feeling. The emotionally charged delivery and nearby promise are adequately treated as context and as a distinct subsequent undertaking; they create no residual pressure requiring E or O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
      ],
